f so you should definitely use trio for  your next asic project  personal anecdote uh we have  a system that talks to let's encrypt  uh to manage certificates for a cluster  and that's built with twisted because we  built it like  uh five years ago and it worked  great until uh let's encrypt  retired their version one api and the  library we were using didn't support  version two and it was quicker and  easier  to learn trio and re-implement  the whole system in trio from scratch  than it was to try  and update the library to use  the slightly different two api  um and deploy a new version of the thing  we already had  so trio is great  and that's the end
 

